 "valuation": {
  "name": "Valuation calculator",
  "items": [
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.1",
    "kind": "Small label",
    "text": "Valuation calculator"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.2",
    "kind": "Section headline",
    "text": "How would buyers value <em>your business?</em>"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.3",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "Most owners have blind spots about what their business is worth. Answer ten questions and see the range a buyer would start from, in about a minute."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.4",
    "kind": "List item",
    "text": "<b>1</b>Your business"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.5",
    "kind": "List item",
    "text": "<b>2</b>About you"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.6",
    "kind": "List item",
    "text": "<b>3</b>Your range"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.7",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "Your figures stay in your browser through step 1. They are sent to Capital Row together with your contact details when you request the range in step 2."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.8",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Last twelve months revenue"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.9",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Last twelve months adjusted earnings"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.10",
    "kind": "Text",
    "text": "Adjusted earnings: profit before interest, tax, depreciation and amortization, with your own pay above a market salary and one-time costs added back."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.11",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Company type"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.12",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Which brings in more revenue?"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.13",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Yearly earnings growth, last three years"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.14",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Revenue that is repeat or recurring"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.15",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Revenue from your five largest customers"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.16",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Do you sell to a highly regulated industry?"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.17",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Your plans for your own role after a sale"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.18",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Sectors, optional"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.19",
    "kind": "Button",
    "text": "Next"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.20",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Company name"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.21",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Your role"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.22",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "First name"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.23",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Last name"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.24",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Work email"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.25",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Mobile number, optional"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.26",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "When do you plan to sell?"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.27",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "How did you hear about us? Optional"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.28",
    "kind": "Form label",
    "text": "Who, or which one"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.29",
    "kind": "Text",
    "text": "I agree to receive text messages from Capital Row LLC at the mobile number above, such as market updates and event invitations. Consent is not a condition of any engagement."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.30",
    "kind": "Text",
    "text": "Optional."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.31",
    "kind": "Text",
    "text": "Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out, HELP for help. <a>Privacy Policy</a> and <a>SMS Terms</a>."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.32",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "When you press Calculate, your answers and details come to Capital Row, so that we can follow up. <a>Privacy Policy</a>."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.33",
    "kind": "Button",
    "text": "Previous"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.34",
    "kind": "Button",
    "text": "Calculate"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.35",
    "kind": "Small label",
    "text": "What a buyer will look at"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.36",
    "kind": "Small label",
    "text": "What moves the range"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.37",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "A buyer prices the earnings it can support with documents. Every added-back item you cannot document comes off your earnings before any multiple is applied. A Pre-Market Assessment reads your numbers the way a buyer will, before a buyer does."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.38",
    "kind": "Button",
    "text": "Book a consultation"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.39",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "Twenty minutes, confidential, on a Pre-Market Assessment for your business. <a>Request a Pre-Market Assessment</a>"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.40",
    "kind": "Text",
    "text": "Your earnings or your revenue"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.41",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "Services businesses are priced on adjusted earnings. Software is usually priced on revenue."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.42",
    "kind": "Text",
    "text": "Published figures"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.43",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "For software, the median and the average of private SaaS transactions from Software Equity Group; the listed SaaS index is shown apart, for reference. For services, the published multiple for companies of your earnings size."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.44",
    "kind": "Text",
    "text": "Your range"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.45",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "Software: from the median to the average. Services: your adjusted earnings at the multiple for your size. A buyer sets the price after diligence of your records."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.46",
    "kind": "Button",
    "text": "Change my answers"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.47",
    "kind": "Note",
    "text": "Illustrative market range. Actual value depends on business performance, financial quality and deal terms."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.48",
    "kind": "Text",
    "text": "Sources and methodology"
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.49",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "The range is an educational estimate from your own answers and published figures. It is not a valuation, an appraisal or an offer, and it is not financial, tax or legal advice. It does not account for the specific factors that can change what a buyer pays. For an accurate view, speak with a qualified advisor."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.50",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "Software: <a>Software Equity Group, 2Q26 SaaS M&A and Public Market Report</a>. The range runs from the median, 4.0 times, to the average, 6.2 times, enterprise value to trailing twelve months revenue across disclosed private SaaS transactions in the quarter (page 8). The SEG SaaS Index median, 3.2 times (page 22), is listed companies, a different population: it is shown for reference and is not part of the range. For software + services, the software reading applies to the recurring revenue you report."
   },
   {
    "key": "sh.valuation.51",
    "kind": "Paragraph",
    "text": "Services: your adjusted earnings times the multiple for your earnings size in <a>Pepperdine Graziadio Business School, 2026 Private Capital Markets Report</a> (Spring 2026), Table 31, page 66, business services, multiples of earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortization: under $1M, 4.8 times; $1M to $4.99M, 6.2 times; $5M to $9.99M, 6.5 times; $10M to $24.99M, 7.5 times; $25M and over, 7.0 times. 43 investment bankers, on transactions closed in the twelve months before January 2026. The table labels these figures medians and the report text calls them averages, so the calculator calls them published multiples. The same table is used for every services business, including transportation and logistics. For software + services, the services reading applies to your adjusted earnings and the software reading to your recurring revenue."
   }
  ]
